          ":question/id": "90e895ee-1be8-55c1-ab2d-a3596627f1b5",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-97487",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-4x{y}^{2}$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "First, we define $f(x,y)=-4x{y}^{2}.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/96/96c937cf10d45d8870a4a56e257d184dcf2e4caf11312c05df9f385f9c5ee7a8.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement \u201cAt every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\u201d is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement \u201cAt every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\u201d is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement \u201cAt every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\u201d is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant."
        }
      ],
